    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0403" n="343" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg343"/>

                <head>Mr. McCook to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 57.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Honolulu,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-09-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 4, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to call the attention of
                    the honorable Secretary of State to the inclosed copy of a dispatch with its
                    inclosures, which I have received from his Hawaiian Majesty’s minister of
                    foreign affairs in reply to my communication to him concerning the coolie trade,
                    a copy of which I forwarded to you in my dispatch No. 54, dated August 14,
                    1868.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>EDWARD M. McCOOK.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>







